# FigureAtlas

Use this rule when a paper, slide, poster, or video frame needs a chart, diagram, map, or illustration.

Source catalog: https://github.com/TardisBooo/figureatlas

## Steps

1. Pick the frame: journal single column, journal double column, 16:9 slide, 4:3 slide, A0 poster, or 1080p video.
2. Open `CATALOG.md` and pick one existing figure id. The catalog has 300 verified types. Do not invent a 301st type.
3. Call `render_figure(id)` from `figureatlas.py`.
4. Export HTML or SVG. Check the matching screenshot under `assets/gallery/atlas/` before treating the export as final.

## Credit

The catalog and the 300 verified screenshots are from TardisBooo/figureatlas, Apache-2.0.
